  "description": "One candle takes out both the external high and the external low and closes bearish. No bullish break is recorded.",
  "labelling_rationale": "s4-close-through-breaks-structure-a-wick-does-not, with its break candle widened into an outside bar and turned red.\n\n3.5 edge case (1): 'one candle closes beyond both an external high and low (extreme outside bar): resolve by close direction -- bullish close => bullish BOS only; the opposite penetration becomes a sweep candidate.'\n\nThe engine did not implement it. `_replay_bos` took its direction and its candidate swing kind from the trend state alone and never read the close's own direction, so a candle could only break the way the trend already pointed. Settled by the developer 2026-08-23.\n\nIndex 301 opens at 78 and closes at 70. Its high of 79 clears the external high at 288, price 67; its low of 50 undercuts the external low at 294, price 53. Both extremes are taken by the one candle, so only one of them can be the break -- and the body is bearish.\n\nSo no BOS_UP is recorded, and that absence is the assertion. Its parent series closes at 68 on the same candle with a bullish body and does break, so the two together isolate the body as the only thing that differs.\n\nThe break is withheld rather than replaced by a bearish one. 3.5's main rule requires 'the trend agreeing' and the trend here is BULLISH, so a bearish BOS cannot satisfy both clauses at once; the doctrine contradicts itself in this corner and this is the reading both halves survive. Edge case (1) sends the downward penetration to the Liquidity Engine as a sweep candidate, which is where sweeps are recorded anyway, so nothing is lost.\n\nThe close of 70 clears the level by 3, comfortably outside any 0.05 x ATR band even with the wide range this candle adds to the ATR -- so epsilon is not what withholds the break here, and the case tests what it says it does.",
  "labelled_by": "drafted by Claude Opus 5 2026-08-23 from SLS 3.5 edge case (1), on the developer's ruling of the same date; PENDING DEVELOPER VERIFICATION -- same method and the same parent series as the nine signed off on 2026-08-23",
  "labelled_at": "2026-08-23",
